  "family": "jazz",
  "lineage": "Earliest documented jazz style (c.1905-1928) emerging from New Orleans through cornet-led front-line (cornet/trumpet, clarinet, trombone) playing collective polyphonic improvisation over banjo/guitar-bass-drums rhythm section. Original Dixieland Jass Band's 1917 Livery Stable Blues was the first commercial jazz recording. Distinguished from later swing era by Dixieland's collective-improvisation (vs solo-feature) ensemble principle and 2/4 march-derived rhythmic pulse.",
